---
layout: base.njk
comments: true
commentsCategory: lore
---
<article class="codex-entry" data-codex-category="{{ category }}">
  <header class="codex-entry__header">
    <nav class="codex-breadcrumb" aria-label="Codex location" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <ol class="breadcrumb" role="list">
        <li><a href="/star-rangers/codex/">Codex</a></li>
        {% if category %}
        <li>{{ category | title }}</li>
        {% endif %}
        <li aria-current="page">{{ title }}</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="codex-entry__title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if category %}
    <p class="codex-entry__category">Category: <strong>{{ category }}</strong></p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if author or institution %}
    <p class="codex-entry__byline">
      {% if author %}Author: <strong>{{ author }}</strong>{% endif %}
      {% if author and institution %} — {% endif %}
      {% if institution %}Institution: <strong>{{ institution }}</strong>{% endif %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if location %}
    <p class="codex-entry__byline">Physical record: <strong>{{ location }}</strong></p>
    {% endif %}
    {#-
      Says out loud, on the entry itself, what the Codex index only implies to
      a reader who arrived through it - and most don't: a search result, a
      cross-link from a lore page, or an external citation all land here
      directly. The four canon statuses are the easiest thing on this site to
      flatten, and flattening them turns a named source's account into the
      Archive stating fact. `author` is required on every codex entry for this
      exact reason (lib/content-schema.js), so the notice can always name
      someone to attribute the claims to.
    -#}
    {#- data-pagefind-ignore for the same reason the breadcrumb and footer
        carry it: identical boilerplate on all 32 codex entries would
        otherwise put 32 indistinguishable hits behind a search for
        "primary source" or "canon". -#}
    <aside class="codex-entry__status" aria-label="How to read this document" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <p><strong>A primary source, not the Archive's own voice.</strong>
      This document is canon <em>for its author</em>: it records what
      {% if author %}{{ author }}{% else %}its author{% endif %} set down, by their own lights and with their own
      blind spots. It may be partial, self-serving, or contradicted by
      <a href="/star-rangers/lore/">settled lore</a>, by a chapter, or by
      another codex entry. Cite it as an account, not as established fact.</p>
    </aside>
    {% if tags and tags.length %}
    <ul class="chapter-tags" aria-label="Tags" role="list">
      {% for tag in tags %}
      <li class="chapter-tag">{{ tag }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if image %}
    <img class="entry-image" src="/star-rangers/images/codex/{{ image }}" alt="{{ image_alt | default(title) }}" />
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <div class="codex-entry__body">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>

  <footer class="codex-entry__footer" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <a href="/star-rangers/codex/">← Back to Codex</a>
  </footer>
</article>
